---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import CapitalGainsTaxCalculator from "../../../components/CapitalGainsTaxCalculator.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Capital Gains Tax Calculator (Canada) | CRA Inclusion Rates"
  description="Estimate your Canadian capital gains tax liability. Automatically applies the 50% inclusion rate and provincial tax brackets."
  ogImage="https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/images/og-capital-gains-tax.png"
>
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/capital-gains-tax-calculator/" slot="head" />
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="en-us" href="https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/capital-gains-tax-calculator/" slot="head" />
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="en-gb" href="https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/capital-gains-tax-calculator/uk/" slot="head" />
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="en-ca" href="https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/capital-gains-tax-calculator/canada/" slot="head" />
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="en-au" href="https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/capital-gains-tax-calculator/australia/" slot="head" />

  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline slot="head">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "FinanceApplication",
        "name": "Capital Gains Tax Calculator (Canada)",
        "applicationCategory": "FinanceApplication",
        "operatingSystem": "Web",
        "provider": { "@id": "https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/#organization" },
        "offers": { "@type": "Offer", "price": "0", "priceCurrency": "CAD" },
        "description": "Estimate Canadian capital gains tax liability with 50% inclusion rate and provincial tax brackets."
      },
      {
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "What is the capital gains inclusion rate in Canada?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Historically, 50% of your capital gain is included in your taxable income. The 2024 Federal Budget introduced a two-tiered system for amounts exceeding $250,000."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "How does the Canadian Principal Residence Exemption (PRE) protect home sales from tax?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "The PRE allows Canadian residents to eliminate capital gains tax on the sale of their primary home for every year the property was designated as their principal residence, providing 100% tax-free capital growth."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "What is the Superficial Loss Rule under CRA regulations?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "The CRA Superficial Loss Rule denies a capital loss deduction if you (or an affiliated person) repurchase the same or identical asset within 30 calendar days before or after the sale. The denied loss is added to the cost basis of the new asset instead."
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
  </script>

  <main class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <div class="mb-8 text-center sm:text-left">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight font-sans">
        Capital Gains Tax Calculator (Canada)
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400 max-w-3xl">
        Estimate your CRA capital gains tax liability with automatic inclusion rate calculations and provincial tax bracket modeling.
      </p>
    </div>

    <CapitalGainsTaxCalculator defaultCountry="CA" />

    <!-- Explanatory Content Wrapper -->
    <div class="mt-12 space-y-8 text-slate-300">
      <!-- Introduction Section -->
      <section class="glass-panel p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl space-y-4">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[#00F5D4]/10 text-[#00F5D4] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border border-[#00F5D4]/20">
          <span>CRA Tax Framework</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Introduction</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          Capital gains taxation in Canada operates on a distinct <strong>inclusion rate</strong> mechanism rather than separate capital gains tax rate schedules. Under Canada Revenue Agency (CRA) tax law, only a specific percentage—the statutory inclusion rate (50%, with recent federal budget proposals introducing a 66.67% rate for individual gains exceeding $250,000)—of your net capital gain is included in your taxable income. The taxable portion is then added directly to your ordinary annual income and taxed at your combined federal and provincial marginal tax rate. This calculator evaluates your total CRA tax obligation, applying the exact inclusion rate and provincial brackets to measure your net after-tax proceeds.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Key Benefits Section -->
      <section class="glass-panel p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl space-y-4">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[#7B61FF]/10 text-[#7B61FF] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border border-[#7B61FF]/20">
          <span>Strategic Value</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Key Benefits</h2>
        <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 pt-2">
          <li class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-[#00F5D4] font-bold mt-0.5">•</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Calculate CRA Capital Gains Inclusion Rates</strong>
              <span class="text-sm text-slate-400">Apply the statutory 50% inclusion rate (and high-income $250,000 threshold rates) to compute taxable gains.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-[#00F5D4] font-bold mt-0.5">•</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Model Combined Federal & Provincial Tax Rates</strong>
              <span class="text-sm text-slate-400">Estimate tax friction across all Canadian provinces and territories based on your marginal tax bracket.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-[#00F5D4] font-bold mt-0.5">•</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Apply Principal Residence Exemption (PRE)</strong>
              <span class="text-sm text-slate-400">Confirm 100% tax exemption on capital gains realized from the sale of your primary home.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-[#00F5D4] font-bold mt-0.5">•</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Incorporate Capital Loss Offsets</strong>
              <span class="text-sm text-slate-400">Apply net capital losses against gains realized in the current year, 3 prior years, or carry forward indefinitely.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- FAQ Section -->
      <section class="glass-panel p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl space-y-6">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[#00F5D4]/10 text-[#00F5D4] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border border-[#00F5D4]/20">
          <span>Common Questions</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] overflow-hidden">
            <button 
              type="button"
              onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('hidden'); this.querySelector('svg').classList.toggle('rotate-180');" 
              class="w-full p-4 sm:p-5 text-left font-semibold text-white flex items-center justify-between gap-4 hover:bg-slate-900/50 transition-colors focus:outline-none"
            >
              <span>What is the capital gains inclusion rate in Canada?</span>
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-[#00F5D4] shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
            <div class="hidden p-4 sm:p-5 pt-0 text-sm text-slate-300 border-t border-[#1E294B]/50 leading-relaxed">
              Historically, 50% of your capital gain is included in your taxable income. The 2024 Federal Budget introduced a two-tiered system for amounts exceeding $250,000.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] overflow-hidden">
            <button 
              type="button"
              onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('hidden'); this.querySelector('svg').classList.toggle('rotate-180');" 
              class="w-full p-4 sm:p-5 text-left font-semibold text-white flex items-center justify-between gap-4 hover:bg-slate-900/50 transition-colors focus:outline-none"
            >
              <span>How does the Canadian Principal Residence Exemption (PRE) protect home sales from tax?</span>
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-[#00F5D4] shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
            <div class="hidden p-4 sm:p-5 pt-0 text-sm text-slate-300 border-t border-[#1E294B]/50 leading-relaxed">
              The PRE allows Canadian residents to eliminate capital gains tax on the sale of their primary home for every year the property was designated as their principal residence, providing 100% tax-free capital growth.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] overflow-hidden">
            <button 
              type="button"
              onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('hidden'); this.querySelector('svg').classList.toggle('rotate-180');" 
              class="w-full p-4 sm:p-5 text-left font-semibold text-white flex items-center justify-between gap-4 hover:bg-slate-900/50 transition-colors focus:outline-none"
            >
              <span>What is the Superficial Loss Rule under CRA regulations?</span>
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-[#00F5D4] shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
            <div class="hidden p-4 sm:p-5 pt-0 text-sm text-slate-300 border-t border-[#1E294B]/50 leading-relaxed">
              The CRA Superficial Loss Rule denies a capital loss deduction if you (or an affiliated person) repurchase the same or identical asset within 30 calendar days before or after the sale. The denied loss is added to the cost basis of the new asset instead.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Methodology Section -->
      <section class="glass-panel p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl space-y-4">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[#7B61FF]/10 text-[#7B61FF] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border border-[#7B61FF]/20">
          <span>Calculation Logic</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Methodology</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            This calculator computes net capital gains under the Canadian Income Tax Act by subtracting your Adjusted Cost Base (ACB) and outlays/expenses from total disposal proceeds. It then multiplies the net gain by the statutory inclusion rate (50% for standard individual gains) to calculate the taxable capital gain portion.
          </p>
          <p>
            The taxable gain is added to line 12700 of your personal T1 income tax return, where it is taxed at your combined federal and provincial marginal tax rates. The model accounts for allowable capital loss deductions, which can offset taxable gains in the current year, carry back 3 years, or carry forward indefinitely.
          </p>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] text-xs text-slate-400 space-y-2">
            <p><strong>Official Reference:</strong> <a href="https://www.canada.ca/en/revenue-agency/services/tax/individuals/topics/about-your-tax-return/tax-return/completing-a-tax-return/deductions-credits-expenses/line-12700-capital-gains.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#00F5D4] hover:underline font-medium">CRA Guide to Line 12700 (Capital Gains) →</a></p>
            <p class="italic text-slate-500">Calculations are estimates, consult a Canadian CPA or licensed tax professional for personal capital gains tax advice.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Related Calculators Section -->
      <section class="space-y-4 pt-4">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Related Calculators & Tools</h3>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
          <a href="/tax-loss-harvesting-calculator/canada/" class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] hover:border-[#00F5D4]/40 transition-all space-y-2 group">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold text-[#00F5D4] uppercase">Canadian Loss Rules</span>
            <h4 class="text-base font-bold text-white group-hover:text-[#00F5D4] transition-colors">Canadian Tax-Loss Harvesting Calculator</h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">Directly offset Canadian capital gains while navigating CRA superficial loss rules.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/buy-borrow-die-calculator/canada/" class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] hover:border-[#7B61FF]/40 transition-all space-y-2 group">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold text-[#7B61FF] uppercase">Canadian Wealth Strategy</span>
            <h4 class="text-base font-bold text-white group-hover:text-[#7B61FF] transition-colors">Canadian Buy, Borrow, Die Calculator</h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">Model asset-backed margin lending strategies to defer Canadian capital gains inclusion.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/rmd-calculator/canada/" class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] hover:border-[#00F5D4]/40 transition-all space-y-2 group">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold text-[#00F5D4] uppercase">Canadian RRIF Rules</span>
            <h4 class="text-base font-bold text-white group-hover:text-[#00F5D4] transition-colors">RRIF Minimum Withdrawal Calculator (Canada)</h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">Calculate mandatory CRA annual RRIF minimum withdrawal percentages.</p>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
